```markdown
---
applyTo: "**/*.{js,ts,json}"
description: "Financial Times Visual Vocabulary chart selection guidelines"
---

## Chart Type Selection Matrix

Based on data relationship, select appropriate visualization: 

### Deviation (variations from reference point) 
- **Use**: Diverging bar charts, spine charts
- **Pattern**: Center baseline, positive/negative values
- **Example**: Budget surplus/deficit, temperature anomalies

### Correlation (relationships between variables)   
- **Use**: Scatterplots, connected scatterplots
- **Pattern**: Two quantitative variables
- **Example**: Income vs. life expectancy, price vs. demand

### Ranking (ordered position more important than absolute value) 
- **Use**: Horizontal bar charts (easier label reading)
- **Pattern**: Ordered categorical data
- **Example**: Top 10 companies by revenue

### Distribution (values and frequency) 
- **Use**: Histograms, box plots
- **Pattern**: Single variable frequency analysis
- **Example**: Income distribution, test score ranges

### Change Over Time 
- **Use**: Line charts, area charts
- **Pattern**: Temporal x-axis
- **Example**: Stock prices, population growth

### Part-to-Whole (component breakdown) 
- **Use**: Stacked bar charts, treemaps
- **Pattern**: Categories summing to total
- **Example**: Budget allocation, market share

### Magnitude (size comparisons) 
- **Use**: Column charts, lollipop charts
- **Pattern**: Comparing absolute values
- **Example**: Country populations, sales by region

## Implementation Examples

### Horizontal Bar Chart (preferred over pie)
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "mark": {"type": "bar", "stroke": "white", "strokeWidth": 1},
  "encoding": {
    "y": {"field": "category", "type": "nominal", "sort": "-x"},
    "x": {"field": "value", "type": "quantitative"},
    "color": {
      "field": "category",
      "type": "nominal", 
      "scale": {"range": ["#4477AA", "#EE6677", "#228833", "#CCBB44"]}
    }
  }
}